{"name":"Hot Shot","hex":"#ec4f28","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hot shot","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of hotshot.","Round shot that has been heated to a glow before firing in order to set wooden enemy ships afire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hot_shot"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heated shot","blocks":[{"text":"Heated shot or hot shot is round shot that is heated before firing from muzzle-loading cannons, for the purpose of setting fire to enemy warships, buildings, or equipment. The use of heated shot dates back centuries. It was a powerful weapon against wooden warships, where fire was always a hazard. It was rendered obsolete in the mid-19th century when vessels armored with iron replaced wooden warships in the world's navies. Also at around the same time, the replacement of solid-iron shot with exploding shells gave artillery a far more destructive projectile that could be fired immediately without preparation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg/330px-Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heated_shot","wikidata":"Q14946777"},{"title":"Hot Shot (Shaggy album)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Shot is the fifth studio album released by Jamaican-American singer Shaggy. The album was first released on 8 August 2000, in the United States, before being issued in the United Kingdom on 9 October 2000, with a revised track listing. The revised UK edition was also released in Europe, but without the song \"Why You Mad at Me?\". The album was reissued in the UK on 26 March 2001. Hot Shot went on to be certified six-times platinum in the United States by the RIAA, and was the second best-selling album of 2001 in that country. The album has sold over nine million copies worldwide. A remix album, titled Hot Shot Ultramix, was released in June 2002. Four singles were released from the album: \"It Wasn't Me\", \"Angel\", \"Luv Me, Luv Me\" and the double A-side single \"Dance & Shout / Hope\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bd/Shaggy_hotshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Shot_(Shaggy_album)","wikidata":"Q1402479"},{"title":"Hot Shot (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Hot Shot is a Taiwanese drama starring Jerry Yan of F4, Show Lo, and Wu Chun of Fahrenheit. It was produced by Comic International Productions and directed by Lin He Long."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/6e/Hot_Shot-Poster.png/330px-Hot_Shot-Poster.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hot_Shot_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q715353"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg/500px-Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg/1280px-Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg/500px-Red-hot_shot_furnace.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mobile furnace, operated by the Royal Norwegian Navy, used to heat cannon shots (ca. 1860).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed-hot_shot_furnace.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Vue_du_siege_de_Gibraltar_et_explosion_des_batteries_flottantes_1782.jpeg/500px-Vue_du_siege_de_Gibraltar_et_explosion_des_batteries_flottantes_1782.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Vue_du_siege_de_Gibraltar_et_explosion_des_batteries_flottantes_1782.jpeg/1280px-Vue_du_siege_de_Gibraltar_et_explosion_des_batteries_flottantes_1782.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Vue_du_siege_de_Gibraltar_et_explosion_des_batteries_flottantes_1782.jpeg/500px-Vue_du_siege_de_Gibraltar_et_explosion_des_batteries_flottantes_1782.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A contemporary aquatint of the 1782 Franco-Spanish attack on Gibraltar. A Spanish floating battery is shown exploding after the British defenders set it on fire with heated shot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVue_du_siege_de_Gibraltar_et_explosion_des_batteries_flottantes_1782.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Iron_furnace_for_heating_iron_shot_during_the_Great_Siege%2C_Gibraltar_Museum.jpg/500px-Iron_furnace_for_heating_iron_shot_during_the_Great_Siege%2C_Gibraltar_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Iron_furnace_for_heating_iron_shot_during_the_Great_Siege%2C_Gibraltar_Museum.jpg/1280px-Iron_furnace_for_heating_iron_shot_during_the_Great_Siege%2C_Gibraltar_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Iron_furnace_for_heating_iron_shot_during_the_Great_Siege%2C_Gibraltar_Museum.jpg/500px-Iron_furnace_for_heating_iron_shot_during_the_Great_Siege%2C_Gibraltar_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An iron grate for heating iron shot during the Great Siege of Gibraltar (1779–83)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIron_furnace_for_heating_iron_shot_during_the_Great_Siege%2C_Gibraltar_Museum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu